<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <%- include('partials/head') %>
  <style>
    .legal-body { background: var(--color-pearl); min-height: 100vh; }
    .legal-page { max-width: 720px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 2.5rem 1.5rem 5rem; }
    .legal-back {
      display: inline-block; font-family: var(--font-body); font-size: 0.85rem;
      font-weight: 400; color: var(--color-bloem); text-decoration: none; margin-bottom: 2rem;
    }
    .legal-back:hover { opacity: 0.7; }
    .legal-title {
      font-family: var(--font-display); font-size: 2.4rem; font-weight: 400;
      color: var(--color-ink-stained); margin: 0 0 0.4rem; line-height: 1.12;
    }
    .legal-updated {
      font-family: var(--font-body); font-size: 0.85rem; font-weight: 300;
      color: rgba(16, 15, 16, 0.55); margin: 0 0 2.25rem;
    }
    .legal-page h2 {
      font-family: var(--font-display); font-size: 1.4rem; font-weight: 400;
      color: var(--color-ink-stained); margin: 2.5rem 0 0.75rem; line-height: 1.2;
    }
    .legal-page h3 {
      font-family: var(--font-body); font-size: 0.98rem; font-weight: 700;
      color: var(--color-ink-stained); margin: 1.5rem 0 0.4rem;
    }
    .legal-page p, .legal-page li {
      font-family: var(--font-body); font-size: 1rem; font-weight: 300;
      line-height: 1.7; color: rgba(16, 15, 16, 0.82);
    }
    .legal-page p { margin: 0 0 1rem; }
    .legal-page ul { margin: 0 0 1rem; padding-left: 1.35rem; }
    .legal-page li { margin-bottom: 0.5rem; }
    .legal-page a { color: var(--color-bloem); text-underline-offset: 2px; }
    .legal-footer {
      margin-top: 3rem; padding-top: 1.5rem; border-top: 1px solid rgba(112, 92, 108, 0.15);
      font-family: var(--font-body); font-size: 0.85rem; font-weight: 300; color: rgba(16, 15, 16, 0.5);
    }
    @media (max-width: 560px) { .legal-title { font-size: 1.9rem; } }
  </style>
</head>
<body class="legal-body">
  <main class="legal-page">
    <a href="/" class="legal-back">← Back</a>

    <h1 class="legal-title">Accessibility Statement</h1>
    <p class="legal-updated">Last updated: August 9, 2026</p>

    <p>
      The Creative's Garden, run by The Meibos Touch (Julia Meibos), is committed to being
      usable by as many people as possible, including people who use assistive technologies.
      This is a small, growing platform, and accessibility is something we keep working on
      rather than treat as finished.
    </p>

    <h2>What we aim for</h2>
    <p>
      We aim to meet the Web Content Accessibility Guidelines (WCAG) 2.1 at Level AA as our
      standard. We don't claim perfect conformance yet, but it's the target we build toward.
    </p>

    <h2>What we've done</h2>
    <p>
      Some of the steps we've taken to make the platform more accessible:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>Structured pages with meaningful, semantic HTML and headings.</li>
      <li>Support for keyboard navigation, with visible focus styles on interactive elements.</li>
      <li>Labels and descriptive text for buttons, links, and form fields.</li>
      <li>Attention to color contrast for body text against its background.</li>
      <li>Respect for the "reduce motion" setting — animations (like the block-buster and
        propagation celebrations) are softened or turned off when your device requests it.</li>
      <li>Responsive layouts that adapt to phones, tablets, and desktops, and to text
        resizing and zoom.</li>
      <li>Alternative text on meaningful images, and decorative images marked so screen
        readers can skip them.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Known limitations</h2>
    <p>
      We're honest that some areas aren't fully there yet. As we add features quickly, a few
      interactive elements, illustrations, or newer sections may not yet meet our standard.
      If you hit a barrier, we'd genuinely like to know so we can fix it.
    </p>

    <h2>Tell us about a problem</h2>
    <p>
      If you have trouble using any part of The Creative's Garden, or you need something in a
      different format, please email
      <a href="mailto:julia@meibostouch.com">julia@meibostouch.com</a>. Let us know the page
      or feature, what happened, and the device or assistive technology you were using if you
      can. We take this seriously and will do our best to help and to improve.
    </p>

    <h2>Updates</h2>
    <p>
      We'll revisit this statement as the platform grows and as we make improvements, and
      we'll update the "last updated" date above.
    </p>

    <p class="legal-footer">
      The Creative's Garden — a content creation course by The Meibos Touch.
    </p>
  </main>
</body>
</html>
